  "font_width_review": {
    "pdf_reference": "PDF Reference 1.6, Appendix H implementation note 60, printed pages 1014-1015",
    "finding": "The PDF format reference requires width consistency; it does not prescribe nearest-integer rounding nor a numeric tolerance. A +1 comparison against a nearest-integer audit is not by itself proof of a PDF/X failure. Floor scaling differs from the exact rational advance by less than one PDF glyph unit; nearest scaling can reduce that error but also does not exactly preserve a fractional advance. No shared worker change is made solely to satisfy that comparator. This is not a normative approval of arbitrary quantization or of the separate CFF-width agreement issue.",
